      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per the bug, this is a significant reduction in charge current. Does it still meet our HW requirements for charging performance? I think it may, but I want to confirm that the testing was done.\n\n* A battery must take no longer than 4 hours to charge from 0 to 100% in the Active state (ACPI S0) at average load. (Average load is measured via average power consumption of power_LoadTest on the platform.)\n\n* A battery must take no longer than 3 hours to charge from 0 to 100% in the Suspend state (ACPI S3).\n\n* A battery must take no longer than 3 hours to charge from 0 to 100% in the Deep Sleep state (ACPI S5).",
      "revId": "987f04b89e1e109ba9542f0aa435e67b39409946",
